| `patient_id` | `P-0123` | direct identifier | RESTRICTED | pseudonymised with HMAC-SHA256 |
| `zip_code` | `123-4567` | quasi-identifier | RESTRICTED | generalised to prefecture |
| `diagnosis` | `E11` | sensitive attribute | RESTRICTED | kept, access controlled |
| `age` | `73` | quasi-identifier | RESTRICTED | binned to 10-year bands |

## Rules of thumb

- Direct identifiers (names, IDs, addresses, e-mail, phone) never leave
  RESTRICTED storage; they are dropped or pseudonymised at the first step.
- Quasi-identifiers (dates, zip codes, rare values) are generalised or
  binned until the k-anonymity target in `DEIDENTIFICATION.md` is met.
- Any derived extract is ANONYMIZED EXTRACT only after the pre-transfer
  checklist has been signed off — pseudonymised data is *not* anonymous.
